{"count":1095,"next":"https://api.afp.mil.ph/articles/?page=11&page_size=100","previous":"https://api.afp.mil.ph/articles/?page=9&page_size=100","results":[{"id":1106,"title":"Philippines, Japan and US hold Trilateral Security Talks","slug":"philippines-japan-and-us-hold-trilateral-security-talks","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong><b><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/TJST_2.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/TJST_2.jpg\" /></b></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong><b>MANILA, Philippines.</b></strong> Defense Forces Planners from the Armed Forces of the Philippines, MGen Jeffrey Hechanova, Japan Self-Defense Forces RAdm Hiroshi Egawa and United States Indo-Pacific Command BGen Jennifer Short met last July 13 for the Trilateral Joint Staff Talks (TJST). Said engagement aims to strengthen the trilateral security partnerships of the Philippines, Japan and the US.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/TJST_2.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-21T11:07:00+08:00","hits":251},{"id":1107,"title":"Philippines, Japan agree to deepen Security Partnerships","slug":"philippines-japan-agree-to-deepen-security-partnerships","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong><b><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/MCWG_1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/MCWG_1.jpg\" /></b></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong><b>Manila, Philippines.</b></strong> The Deputy Chief of Staff for Plans, Armed Forces of the Philippines, MGen Jeffrey C. Hechanova and Director-General, Defense Plans and Policy Department, Japan Self-Defense Forces, RAdm Hiroshi Egawa held the 3<sup>rd</sup> AFP-JSDF Military Cooperation Working Group Staff Talks on July 14-15, 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/MCWG_1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-21T10:59:24+08:00","hits":277},{"id":1108,"title":"Philippine Navy's BRP Antonio Luna tests firepower during RIMPAC live-fire exercise","slug":"philippine-navys-brp-antonio-luna-tests-firepower-during-rimpac-live-fire-exercise","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/80327169-06A2-4B42-A42D-9ECDAA46F0B7.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"450\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/80327169-06A2-4B42-A42D-9ECDAA46F0B7.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Philippine Navy tested the BRP Antonio Luna's (FF151) anti-submarine and main battery capabilities in the Rim of the Pacific (RIMPAC) exercise held in Hawaii from July 12 to 16.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/80327169-06A2-4B42-A42D-9ECDAA46F0B7.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-20T11:11:54+08:00","hits":195},{"id":1109,"title":"LtGen Centino Convenes first Command Conference as AFP Chief","slug":"ltgen-centino-convenes-first-command-conference-as-afp-chief","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Article 5.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Article 5.jpg\" /></strong></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, QUEZON CITY -</strong> The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) held a Command Conference on Saturday Nov 13, 2021, a day after the new Chief of Staff, Lieutenant General Andres Centino assumed his post.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">LtGen Centino met with the top AFP commanders and principal staff officers at the AFP Commissioned Officers’ Country at Camp Aguinaldo to deliver his initial marching orders.<span class=\"mce-nbsp-wrap\" contenteditable=\"false\"> </span><span class=\"mce-nbsp-wrap\" contenteditable=\"false\"> </span></span></p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Article%205.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-18T08:58:21+08:00","hits":160},{"id":1110,"title":"Courtesy Call of Brig. Gen. Jennifer M Short USAF","slug":"courtesy-call-of-brig-gen-jennifer-m-short-usaf","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/SHORT4.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/SHORT4.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Brig. Gen. Jennifer M Short USAF, the Deputy Director for Strategic Planning and Policy Directorate of the United States Indo-Pacific Command renders a courtesy call to Vice Admiral Rommel Anthony SD Reyes, The Deputy Chief of Staff Armed Forces of the Philippines (TDCSAFP) at the General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City on Tuesday, 12 July 2022.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Brig. Gen. Short attended the Phil-US Executive Committee Meeting as part of the Mutual Defense Board-Security Engagement Board (MDB-SEB) planning cycle./// (Photo by:  SN1 Donald Viluan PN (Ret)/PAO AFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/SHORT4.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-14T11:17:32+08:00","hits":273},{"id":1111,"title":"Courtesy Call of Rear Admiral Hiroshi Egawa","slug":"courtesy-call-of-rear-admiral-hiroshi-egawa","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/EGA1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/EGA1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Rear Admiral Hiroshi Egawa of the Defense Plans and Policy Department, Japan Self-Defense Forces (JSDF), renders a courtesy call to Vice Admiral Rommel Anthony SD Reyes, The Deputy Chief of Staff Armed Forces of the Philippines (TDCSAFP)at the AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City on Wednesday, 13 July 2022.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">RAdm Egawa is in the country for the AFP-JSDF Military Cooperation Working Group Staff Talks from 14 - 15 July 2022.///<br /><br />(Photo by: SN1 Donald Viluan PN (Ret)/PAO AFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/EGA1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-14T11:15:24+08:00","hits":220},{"id":1115,"title":"General Faustino Jr relinquishes Chief of Staff post to Lt. Gen. Centino","slug":"general-faustino-jr-relinquishes-chief-of-staff-v2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Feat Article 1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Feat Article 1.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City</strong> — General Jose Faustino Jr relinquished his post as Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) in a Joint Change of Command and Retirement Ceremony today, November 12 as he bowed out of service after over 37 years in the military.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Lt. Gen. Andres Centino, the current Commanding General of the Philippine Army, took the helm as the 57th Chief of Staff of the AFP.</span></p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Feat%20Article%201.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:14+08:00","hits":192},{"id":1114,"title":"Army reservists, ROTC assist DSWD in relief effort","slug":"army-reservists-rotc-assist-dswd-in-relief-effort-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Army reservists ROTC assist DSWD in relief effort.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Army reservists ROTC assist DSWD in relief effort.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City </strong>- Philippine Army Reservists and ROTC cadets from the 14th Regional Community Defense Group, assist the DSWD in hauling relief items for victims of the 7.3-magnitude earthquake that hit Northern Luzon on July 27, 2022.</span></p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Army%20reservists%20ROTC%20assist%20DSWD%20in%20relief%20effort.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:14+08:00","hits":142},{"id":1113,"title":"AFP Chief leads demilitarization of firearms","slug":"afp-chief-leads-demilitarization-of-firearms","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feat-story-4.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/feat-story-4.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City </strong>—  The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Chief of Staff General Jose Faustino Jr led the demilitarization of firearms in 4th Infantry Division, on Wednesday, October 27.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">A total of 316 firearms that were captured, confiscated, surrendered and recovered (CCSR) by the troops were properly disposed of. The activity served as the highlight of General Faustino’s farewell visit to 4ID.</span></p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/feat-story-4.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:14+08:00","hits":186},{"id":1112,"title":"AFP activates Office of the Secretariat for Joint Peace Security Coordinating Council","slug":"afp-activates-office-of-the-secretariat","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Article 4.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Article 4.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City </strong>— The Armed Forces of the Philippines activated the Office for the AFP Secretariat, Joint Peace and Security Coordinating Council today, November 8, in a ceremony at the General Headquarters here.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The new Office shall be the focal point for the AFP and will perform secretariat functions for the Chief of Staff, who co-chairs the council along with the Director General of the Philippine National Police and the Commandant of the Philippine Coast Guard.</span></p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Article%204.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:14+08:00","hits":5254},{"id":1135,"title":"MGen Sequitin bows out of military service, Col Aguilar takes command of CRSAFP","slug":"mgen-sequitin-bows-out-of-military-service","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> <img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MGen Sequitin bows out of military service Col Aguilar takes command of CRSAFP.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"586\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/MGen Sequitin bows out of military service Col Aguilar takes command of CRSAFP.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City </strong>- The Commander of the Civil Relations Service, Armed Forces of the Philippines, Maj. Gen. Manuel V Sequitin bowed out of service in a Change of Command and Retirement Ceremony at AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo on Thursday, August 18, after over 37 years of outstanding military service.<span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"> </span></span></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MGen%20Sequitin%20bows%20out%20of%20military%20service%20Col%20Aguilar%20takes%20command%20of%20CRSAFP.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":118},{"id":1134,"title":"AFP reaffirms commitment to IHL","slug":"afp-reaffirms-commitment-to-ihl-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> </span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/AFP reaffirms commitment to IHL.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/AFP reaffirms commitment to IHL.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<p><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City</strong>—The Armed Forces of the Philippines opened on Monday, August 1, its month-long commemoration of the International Humanitarian Law (IHL) with an oath-taking ceremony at the General Headquarters in Quezon City.</p>\r\n<p>Brig. Gen. Joel Alejandro S Nacnac, Director of the AFP Center for Law of Armed Conflict, led the reading of the pledge that reaffirms the AFP’s adherence to the principles of IHL and commitment to its promulgation to all military and civilian personnel.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/AFP%20reaffirms%20commitment%20to%20IHL.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":105},{"id":1133,"title":"AFP joins National IHL Day Commemoration","slug":"afp-joins-national-ihl-day-commemoration-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP joins National IHL Day Commemoration.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/AFP joins National IHL Day Commemoration.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City</strong> – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) joined various government and non-government agencies in the national commemoration of the International Humanitarian Law (IHL) Day on Friday, August 12.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\"> </span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bmgbi-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bmgbi-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"bmgbi-0-0\">The IHL day commemoration ceremony was held at the AFP Commissioned Officers Country in Camp Aguinaldo, with the Department of National Defense (DND) serving as the host. One of the event’s highlights was the opening of a photo exhibit showcasing the importance of IHL and Human Rights.</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bmgbi-0-0\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP%20joins%20National%20IHL%20Day%20Commemoration.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":107},{"id":1132,"title":"AFP flies the Philippine flag at half-staff","slug":"afp-flies-the-philippine-flag-at-half-staff-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP flies the Philippine flag at half-staff.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/AFP flies the Philippine flag at half-staff.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<p>The Armed Forces of the Philippines flies the Philippine flag at half-staff in mourning of former President Fidel V Ramos during the flag-raising ceremony at Camp Aguinaldo in Quezon City on Monday, August 1. AFP officers, enlisted personnel, and civilian human resources wore black bands to commiserate with the passing of the former Commander-in-Chief.</p>\r\n<p>“President Fidel Valdes Ramos left a legacy of leadership, excellence, and sterling public service to the entire Filipino nation. He shall always be remembered with high respect and admiration from his former colleagues, subordinates, and peers,” the AFP announces</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP%20flies%20the%20Philippine%20flag%20at%20half-staff.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":106},{"id":1131,"title":"Philippine Soldier-Athletes dominate 2022 World Eskrima Kali Arnis Championship","slug":"philippine-soldier-athletes-dominate-2022-world-eskrima-kali-arnis-championship-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Philippine Soldier-Athletes dominate 2022 World Eskrima Kali Arnis Championship.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Philippine Soldier-Athletes dominate 2022 World Eskrima Kali Arnis Championship.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<p><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City -</strong> Arnisadors and Eskrimadors from the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) dominated the recently concluded 16th World Eskrima Kali Aris Federation (WEKAF) Championship held in Mandaue City, Cebu from 17-22 July 2022, defeating participants from eight countries.</p>\r\n<p>The AFP sent nine soldier-athletes who contributed 13 gold, eight silver and three bronze medals to the overall medal standing.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Philippine%20Soldier-Athletes%20dominate%202022%20World%20Eskrima%20Kali%20Arnis%20Championship%202.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":110},{"id":1130,"title":"AFP Statement on the passing of Former President Fidel V. Ramos","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-passing-of-former-president-fidel-v-ramos-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/AFP Statement.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/AFP Statement.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<p>The Armed Forces of the Philippines mourns the passing of the 12th President of the Republic of the Philippines, Fidel V. Ramos, who died on Sunday, July 31.</p>\r\n<p>President Ramos dedicated most of his life to the service of our country serving as Chief of the Philippine Constabulary from 1972 to 1986 and Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines from 1986 to 1988. He also headed the Department of National Defense as Secretary from 1988 until 1991.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/AFP%20Statement.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":107},{"id":1129,"title":"Relief Operations","slug":"relief-operations-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Relief Operations.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"601\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Relief Operations.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) utilized its personnel and aircraft assets in distributing relief goods to the seven (7) isolated municipalities of Abra (Boliney, Bucloc, Daguioman, Luba, Tubo, Malibcong, and Lacub) due to the 7.3 magnitude earthquake last July 27.</span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Relief%20Operations.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":107},{"id":1128,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff meets with the Chief of Staff of the United States Air Force","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-meets-with-the-chief-of-staff-of-the-united-states-air-force-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP Chief of Staff meets with the Chief of Staff of the United States Air Force.jpg\" width=\"750\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/AFP Chief of Staff meets with the Chief of Staff of the United States Air Force.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro met with the Chief of Staff of the United States Air Force, General Charles Q Brown Jr, on Wednesday, August 10, during the latter's courtesy call held at the General Headquarters Building in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.</span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP%20Chief%20of%20Staff%20meets%20with%20the%20Chief%20of%20Staff%20of%20the%20United%20States%20Air%20Force.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":113},{"id":1127,"title":"AFP renders full military honors to FVR","slug":"afp-renders-full-military-honors-to-fvr-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP renders full military honors to FVR.jpg\" width=\"700\" height=\"467\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/AFP renders full military honors to FVR.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<p><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City</strong>—The Armed Forces of the Philippines rendered full military honors on Tuesday, August 9, to former president Fidel V Ramos during the state funeral for the 12th President of the Republic of the Philippines.</p>\r\n<p>A battalion-sized contingent of honor guards tendered departure honors for the late president at Heritage Park where he was laid in state.</p>\r\n<p>This was followed by another battalion-sized honor, a funeral march, and a 21-gun salute at the Libingan ng Mga Bayani for his inurnment.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP%20renders%20full%20military%20honors%20to%20FVR.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":133},{"id":1126,"title":"LtGen Bacarro assumes as new Chief of Staff, AFP","slug":"ltgen-bacarro-assumes-as-new-chief-of-staff-afp-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/LtGen Bacarro assumes as new Chief of Staff AFP.jpg\" width=\"640\" height=\"960\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/LtGen Bacarro assumes as new Chief of Staff AFP.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City </strong>- Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro assumed as the new Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, replacing General Andres C Centino on Monday, August 8, in a Change of Command Ceremony presided by President Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">A member of the Philippine Military Academy Maringal Class of 1988, Lt. Gen. Bacarro held command and staff positions that prepared him for his present designation. He is the current commander of Southern Luzon Command (SOLCOM), which covers CALABARZON, MIMAROPA, and Bicol regions. Prior to his stint as SOLCOM Commander, he was the commander of the 2nd Infantry Division, Philippine Army, and Commander of the 502nd Infantry Brigade.</span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/LtGen%20Bacarro%20assumes%20as%20new%20Chief%20of%20Staff%20AFP.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":125},{"id":1125,"title":"Symposium highlights Philippine Air Force's journey to operational and organizational excellence","slug":"symposium-highlights-philippine-air-forces-journey-to-operational-and-organizational-excellence","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Symposium highlights Philippine Air Forces journey to operational and organizational excellence.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Symposium highlights Philippine Air Forces journey to operational and organizational excellence.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, QUEZON CITY </strong>- The Philippine Air Force (PAF) conducted the Air Force Symposium 2022 in Mariott Hotel, Pasay City on June 22 as part of its 75th-anniversary celebration.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The symposium echoes PAF's anniversary theme: \"Leading an Innovative, Progressive, Adaptive and Dependable Air Force for Peace, Security, and Development.\"</span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Symposium%20highlights%20Philippine%20Air%20Forces%20journey%20to%20operational%20and%20organizational%20excellence.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":145},{"id":1124,"title":"AFP Medical Service celebrates 124th Founding Anniversary","slug":"afp-medical-service-celebrates-124th-founding-anniversary","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP Medical Service celebrates 124th Founding Anniversary.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/AFP Medical Service celebrates 124th Founding Anniversary.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City</strong>—The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Medical Service celebrated its 124 years of exceptional service in a ceremony held at the AFP Commissioned Officers Country in Camp Aguinaldo on Thursday, June 23.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The anniversary marked the developments in modernizing AFP medical facilities and equipment and increasing the competence of medical professionals committed to delivering health services to AFP personnel and their dependents.</span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP%20Medical%20Service%20celebrates%20124th%20Founding%20Anniversary.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":112},{"id":1123,"title":"AFP fetes SEA Games athletes, bar passers","slug":"afp-fetes-sea-games-athletes-bar-passers","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/SEAAFP fetes SEA Games athletes bar passers.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/SEAAFP fetes SEA Games athletes bar passers.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City</strong>—The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) gave recognition to soldier-athletes and their coaches who won medals during the 31st South East Asian (SEA) games, and to AFP personnel who passed the latest bar exam in a ceremony at the AFP General Headquarters on Tuesday, June 21.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">AFP Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA led the awarding of 74 military officers, enlisted personnel, and civilian human resources.</span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/SEAAFP%20fetes%20SEA%20Games%20athletes%20bar%20passers.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":155},{"id":1122,"title":"AFP Awards Campaign Battle Streamers to 4ID units","slug":"afp-awards-campaign-battle-streamers-to-4id-units","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP Awards Campaign Battle Streamers to 4ID units.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"486\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/AFP Awards Campaign Battle Streamers to 4ID units.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) awarded the Campaign Battle Streamers to Army units belonging to the 4th Infantry ‘Diamond’ Division in recognition of their achievements against Communist NPA Terrorists (CNTs) on Monday, June 20.</span></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The AFP Chief of Staff, General Andres Centino presided over the awarding ceremony held at the 4ID headquarters in Camp Edilberto Evangelista, Patag, Cagayan de Oro City.</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP%20Awards%20Campaign%20Battle%20Streamers%20to%204ID%20units.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":156},{"id":1121,"title":"AFP Statement on the Appointment of Gen Faustino Jr (Ret) as OIC, DND","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-appointment-of-gen-faustino-jr-ret-as-oic-dnd","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/AFP Statement.jpg\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/AFP Statement.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines welcomes the appointment of retired General Jose C Faustino Jr as officer-in-charge of the Department of National Defense under the Marcos administration.</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/AFP%20Statement.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":126},{"id":1120,"title":"Armor Division celebrates its 46th Anniversary","slug":"armor-division-celebrates-its-46th-anniversary","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Armor Division celebrates its 46th Anniversary.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Armor Division celebrates its 46th Anniversary.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armor (Pambato) Division of the Philippine Army celebrates its 46th founding anniversary in Camp O'Donnell, Capas, Tarlac on Thursday, June 16.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The Commander of the Armor Division Major General Efren Baluyot together with the commanders of various Armor units celebrated the anniversary with the AFP Chief of Staff, General Andres Centino as the Guest of Honor and Speaker.</span></p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Armor%20Division%20celebrates%20its%2046th%20Anniversary.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":155},{"id":1119,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff’s Message on 124th Philippine Independence Day","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-s-message-on-124th-philippine-independence-day","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/BE9B5DBC-04D0-4A00-A0B1-231E15AB6372.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"470\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/BE9B5DBC-04D0-4A00-A0B1-231E15AB6372.jpeg\" /></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Ang buong Sandatahang Lakas ng Pilipinas ay nakikiisa sa sambayanang Pilipino sa paggunita ng ika-isang daan at dalawampu't apat na Araw ng Kalayaan. Mula sa ating mga bayani na nagpamalas ng katapangan at malasakit, ang inyong mga Hukbong Sandatahan na kumakatawan sa mga makabagong bayani ay sumasaludo sa ilang salinlahing Pilipino na nangalaga sa kasarinlan ng Pilipinas.</span></p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/BE9B5DBC-04D0-4A00-A0B1-231E15AB6372.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":121},{"id":1118,"title":"AFP honors retiring PMA Superintendent","slug":"afp-honors-retiring-pma-superintendent","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/AFP honors retiring PMA Superintendent.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/AFP honors retiring PMA Superintendent.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City </strong>– The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) paid tribute to Lieutenant General Ferdinand M Cartujano PAF, Superintendent of the Philippine Military Academy (PMA) with a testimonial parade and review on Tuesday, June 14.</span></p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/AFP%20honors%20retiring%20PMA%20Superintendent.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":154},{"id":1117,"title":"AFP joins 124th Independence Day Commemoration","slug":"afp-joins-124th-independence-day-commemoration","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/AFP joins 124th Independence Day Commemoration.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"578\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/AFP joins 124th Independence Day Commemoration.jpeg\" /></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City </strong>– The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) joined the Filipino nation in celebrating the 124th proclamation of the Philippine Independence this Sunday, June 12.</span></p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/AFP%20joins%20124th%20Independence%20Day%20Commemoration.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":251},{"id":1116,"title":"AFP Statement on the fire incident at the ammo complex inside 4ID","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-fire-incident-at-the-ammo-complex-inside-4id","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/AFP Statement.jpg\" width=\"700\" height=\"700\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/AFP Statement.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<p> </p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 18px;\">A fire incident followed by loud explosions transpired at the Ammo Complex of the 10th Forward Service Support Unit (FSSU), Army Support Command (ASCOM) inside Camp Edilberto Evangelista, Patag, Cagayan de Oro City at past midnight of July 12, 2022.</span></p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/AFP%20Statement.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:12+08:00","hits":199},{"id":1136,"title":"AFP Statement on the fire incident at the ammo complex inside 4ID","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-fire-incident-at-the-ammo-complex-inside-4id-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A fire incident followed by loud explosions transpired at the Ammo Complex of the 10th Forward Service Support Unit (FSSU), Army Support Command (ASCOM) inside Camp Edilberto Evangelista, Patag, Cagayan de Oro City at past midnight of July 12, 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-12T11:20:05+08:00","hits":260},{"id":1137,"title":"AFP Statement on the Celebration of Eid Al-Adha","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-celebration-of-eid-al-adha","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines is one with our Muslim brothers and sisters in the peaceful and joyful observance of Eid al-Adha.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-09T11:21:46+08:00","hits":210},{"id":1140,"title":"REGIONAL PARTNERS","slug":"regional-partners-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> <img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/REGIONAL PARTNERS.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"632\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/REGIONAL PARTNERS.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), Lt. Gen. Bartolome Vicente Bacarro, receives Lt. Gen. Greg Bilton, the Chief of Joint Operations, Australian Defense Force, during his visit and courtesy call at the General Headquarters in Quezon City today, August 18.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/REGIONAL%20PARTNERS.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-08T02:02:12+08:00","hits":109},{"id":1139,"title":"STRENGTHENING PARTNERSHIP","slug":"strengthening-partnership-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> <img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/SA.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"650\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/SA.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), Lt. Gen. Bartolome Vicente Bacarro, meets with the Commander of the United States Pacific Fleet, Admiral Samuel Paparo, on Thursday, August 18.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/SA.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-08T02:02:12+08:00","hits":111},{"id":1138,"title":"Korea Air Force’s 53rd Air Demonstration Group in Basa Air Base","slug":"korea-air-force-s-53rd-air-demonstration-group-in-basa-air-base-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> <img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Korea Air Forces 53rd Air Demonstration Group in Basa Air Base.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"554\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Korea Air Forces 53rd Air Demonstration Group in Basa Air Base.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro attended the Aerobatic Show performed by Republic of Korea Air Force’s 53rd Air Demonstration Group in Basa Air Base, Floridablanca, Pampanga on Monday, August 15.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Korea%20Air%20Forces%2053rd%20Air%20Demonstration%20Group%20in%20Basa%20Air%20Base.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-08T02:02:12+08:00","hits":115},{"id":1141,"title":"ARRIVAL HONORS","slug":"arrival-honors-3","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/AH7.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"583\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/AH7.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines feted the newly-designated Officer-in-Charge of the Department of National Defense, Undersecretary Jose Faustino Jr. with the traditional Arrival Honors on Wednesday, July 6 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AFP Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino served as the Military Host and was accompanied by top AFP and DND officials in welcoming USec. Faustino.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/AH7.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-06T11:26:02+08:00","hits":279},{"id":1142,"title":"Notice of Vacancies","slug":"notice-of-vacancies","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"bi6gxh9e\"><span class=\"d2edcug0 hpfvmrgz qv66sw1b c1et5uql lr9zc1uh jq4qci2q a3bd9o3v b1v8xokw oo9gr5id\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/AA2.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/AA2.jpg\" /></span></div>\r\n<div class=\"bi6gxh9e\"> </div>\r\n<div class=\"bi6gxh9e\"><span class=\"d2edcug0 hpfvmrgz qv66sw1b c1et5uql lr9zc1uh jq4qci2q a3bd9o3v b1v8xokw oo9gr5id\">The Public Affairs Office of the Armed Forces of the Philippines is looking for two qualified individuals to fill-up the following vacant permanent positions:</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"bi6gxh9e\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/AA2.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-04T13:19:32+08:00","hits":678},{"id":1143,"title":"MILITARY CIVIC PARADE","slug":"military-civic-parade","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/PAR1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/PAR1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines displayed its modern assets during the inaugural parade for President Ferdinand Romualdez Marcos Jr at the National Museum in Manila on 30 June 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/PAR1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-01T13:26:01+08:00","hits":784},{"id":1144,"title":"Departure honors for President Ferdinand Romualdez Marcos Jr. as he departs for Malacañan","slug":"departure-honors-for-president-ferdinand-romualdez-marcos-jr-as-he-departs-for-malacanan","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/DEP4.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/DEP4.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines Gen. Andres Centino led the departure honors for the President of the Republic of the Philippines and Commander-in-Chief Ferdinand Romualdez Marcos Jr. as he departs for Malacañan after the inauguration at the National Museum in Manila.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/DEP4.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-01T13:24:16+08:00","hits":350},{"id":1145,"title":"AFP renders departure honors for outgoing Defense Chief","slug":"afp-renders-departure-honors-for-outgoing-defense-chief","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/SND1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/SND1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) rendered departure honors to Secretary Delfin Lorenzana, the outgoing Secretary of the Department of National Defense (DND) on Friday, July 1.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/SND1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-01T13:21:47+08:00","hits":201},{"id":1146,"title":"AFP honors SND Lorenzana with Testimonial Parade","slug":"afp-honors-snd-lorenzana-with-testimonial-parade","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/DND8.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/DND8.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines held a Testimonial Parade and Review on Tuesday, 28 June 2022, in honor of outgoing Secretary of National Defense (SND) Delfin Negrillo Lorenzana.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AFP Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino led the honors as the military recognized the SND’s full support of the AFP’s campaigns and programs.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/DND8.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-29T13:28:25+08:00","hits":351},{"id":1147,"title":"DND approves the activation of the Vice Presidential Security and Protection Group","slug":"dnd-approves-the-activation-of-the-vice-presidential-security-and-protection-group","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/F84F2C16-A40C-4129-8F74-00478021EB96.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/F84F2C16-A40C-4129-8F74-00478021EB96.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Department of National Defense (DND) has approved the activation of the Vice Presidential Security and Protection Group (VPSPG), a dedicated unit that will ensure the safety and security of the Vice President of the Philippines and her family.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In a ceremony held at the AFP General Headquarters on Friday, June 24, AFP Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino led the activation of the VPSPG, which was formerly the Vice Presidential Security Detachment. The Chief of Staff likewise installed Lt. Col. Rene J Giroy PA as the first Group Commander of VPSPG.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/F84F2C16-A40C-4129-8F74-00478021EB96.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-25T13:34:12+08:00","hits":492},{"id":1148,"title":"AFP fetes SEA Games athletes, bar passers ","slug":"afp-fetes-sea-games-athletes-bar-passers-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/SEA.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/SEA.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) gave recognition to soldier-athletes and their coaches who won medals during the 31st South East Asian (SEA) games, and to AFP personnel who passed the latest bar exam in a ceremony at the AFP General Headquarters on Tuesday, June 21.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AFP Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA led the awarding of 74 military officers, enlisted personnel, and civilian human resources.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/SEA.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-24T16:39:28+08:00","hits":438},{"id":1149,"title":" Symposium highlights Philippine Air Force's journey to operational and organizational excellence","slug":"symposium-highlights-philippine-air-forces-journey-to-operational-and-organizational-excellence-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/PAFS3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/PAFS3.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, QUEZON CITY - The Philippine Air Force (PAF) conducted the Air Force Symposium 2022 in Mariott Hotel, Pasay City on June 22 as part of its 75th-anniversary celebration.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The symposium echoes PAF's anniversary theme: \"Leading an Innovative, Progressive, Adaptive and Dependable Air Force for Peace, Security, and Development.\"</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/PAFS3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-24T16:34:51+08:00","hits":433},{"id":1150,"title":"AFP Medical Service celebrates 124th Founding Anniversary","slug":"afp-medical-service-celebrates-124th-founding-anniversary-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/MS9.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/MS9.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Medical Service celebrated its 124 years of exceptional service in a ceremony held at the AFP Commissioned Officers Country in Camp Aguinaldo on Thursday, June 23.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The anniversary marked the developments in modernizing AFP medical facilities and equipment and increasing the competence of medical professionals committed to delivering health services to AFP personnel and their dependents.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/MS9.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-24T16:28:44+08:00","hits":2336},{"id":1151,"title":"AFP Statement on the Appointment of Gen Faustino Jr (Ret) as OIC, DND","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-appointment-of-gen-faustino-jr-ret-as-oic-dnd-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines welcomes the appointment of retired General Jose C Faustino Jr as officer-in-charge of the Department of National Defense under the Marcos administration.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">His over 38 years of military service that culminated in him being the AFP Chief of Staff gave him exclusive and firsthand knowledge of the country's security and defense situation.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP will support General Faustino's plans and programs as we face our country's present and future challenges.///</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-24T16:26:23+08:00","hits":282},{"id":1152,"title":" AFP Awards Campaign Battle Streamers to 4ID units","slug":"afp-awards-campaign-battle-streamers-to-4id-units-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/289382002_387012960127787_871200134010443625_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"486\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/289382002_387012960127787_871200134010443625_n.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) awarded the Campaign Battle Streamers to Army units belonging to the 4th Infantry ‘Diamond’ Division in recognition of their achievements against Communist NPA Terrorists (CNTs) on Monday, June 20.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The AFP Chief of Staff, General Andres Centino presided over the awarding ceremony held at the 4ID headquarters in Camp Edilberto Evangelista, Patag, Cagayan de Oro City.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/289382002_387012960127787_871200134010443625_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-21T16:41:29+08:00","hits":496},{"id":1153,"title":"Armor Division celebrates its 46th Anniversary","slug":"armor-division-celebrates-its-46th-anniversary-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/ARM1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/ARM1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armor (Pambato) Division of the Philippine Army celebrates its 46th founding anniversary in Camp O'Donnell, Capas, Tarlac on Thursday, June 16.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Commander of the Armor Division Major General Efren Baluyot together with the commanders of various Armor units celebrated the anniversary with the AFP Chief of Staff, General Andres Centino as the Guest of Honor and Speaker.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/ARM1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-17T16:43:34+08:00","hits":212},{"id":1154,"title":"AFP honors retiring PMA Superintendent","slug":"afp-honors-retiring-pma-superintendent-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/PMA4.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/PMA4.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) paid tribute to Lieutenant General Ferdinand M Cartujano PAF, Superintendent of the Philippine Military Academy (PMA) with a testimonial parade and review on Tuesday, June 14.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Lieutenant General Cartujano is the 82nd PMA Superintendent who will be retiring on June 26 after 34 years in the military service.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/PMA4.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-15T16:47:37+08:00","hits":230},{"id":1155,"title":"AFP troops discover high-powered firearms in Batangas","slug":"afp-troops-discover-high-powered-firearms-in-batangas","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/E4FA63F6-6634-4666-BA8B-F0593FAB81C4.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/E4FA63F6-6634-4666-BA8B-F0593FAB81C4.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City-Elements from the Philippine Army’s 85th Infantry Battalion and 59th Infantry Battalion discovered an arms cache of high-powered firearms while conducting intelligence operations at Sitio Pinagkawaran, Brgy. Sapangan, San Juan, Batangas, on Friday, June 10.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Seized were one M14 and one Carbine rifles with loaded magazines.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/E4FA63F6-6634-4666-BA8B-F0593FAB81C4.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-12T16:54:24+08:00","hits":252},{"id":1156,"title":"AFP joins 124th Independence Day Commemoration","slug":"afp-joins-124th-independence-day-commemoration-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/4C82A8E6-6283-47BB-8B55-4FED411549FD.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"578\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/4C82A8E6-6283-47BB-8B55-4FED411549FD.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) joined the Filipino nation in celebrating the 124th proclamation of the Philippine Independence this Sunday, June 12.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP has teamed up with the National Historical Commission of the Philippines (NHCP) in the conduct of simultaneous activities within and outside Metro Manila.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/4C82A8E6-6283-47BB-8B55-4FED411549FD.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-12T16:52:25+08:00","hits":180},{"id":1157,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff’s Message on 124th Philippine Independence Day","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-s-message-on-124th-philippine-independence-day-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/BE9B5DBC-04D0-4A00-A0B1-231E15AB6372.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"470\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/BE9B5DBC-04D0-4A00-A0B1-231E15AB6372.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Ang buong Sandatahang Lakas ng Pilipinas ay nakikiisa sa sambayanang Pilipino sa paggunita ng ika-isang daan at dalawampu't apat na Araw ng Kalayaan. Mula sa ating mga bayani na nagpamalas ng katapangan at malasakit, ang inyong mga Hukbong Sandatahan na kumakatawan sa mga makabagong bayani ay sumasaludo sa ilang salinlahing Pilipino na nangalaga sa kasarinlan ng Pilipinas.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/BE9B5DBC-04D0-4A00-A0B1-231E15AB6372.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-12T16:49:55+08:00","hits":328},{"id":1158,"title":" 4th Infantry Battalion clash with Communist NPA Terrorists, seize firearm in Oriental Mindoro ","slug":"4th-infantry-battalion-clash-with-communist-npa-terrorists-seize-firearm-in-oriental-mindoro","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - Elements of the Philippine Army’s 4th Infantry Battalion engaged with the CNT members while conducting focused military operations in Sitio Hagupit, Brgy. Lisap in Bongabong, Oriental Mindoro on Wednesday, June 8.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Following the encounter, troops were able to capture an M14 rifle with magazine and ammunitions, cellular phone, assorted medicines, contraceptive pills, and subversive documents from the enemies.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-10T16:56:17+08:00","hits":178},{"id":1159,"title":"AFP, GMA Kapuso Foundation renew agreement on cooperation","slug":"afp-gma-kapuso-foundation-renew-agreement-on-cooperation","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/220609.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/220609.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines and the GMA Kapuso Foundation, Inc. (GMAKF) renewed for another three years a memorandum of agreement (MOA) institutionalizing their partnership in uplifting the lives of underprivileged Filipinos in geographically isolated and depressed areas (GIDAs).</p>\r\n<p>The agreement, which was first inked in 2016 and again in 2019, was signed by AFP Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA and GMAKF Chairman of the Board of Trustees Atty. Felipe L Gozon through GMAKF Executive Vice President and Chief Operating Officer Ms Luz Annalee Escudero-Catibog today, June 8, at the AFP General Headquarters.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/220609.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-09T17:00:29+08:00","hits":272},{"id":1160,"title":"Visit of Australian Ambassador to AFP General Headquarters","slug":"visit-of-australian-ambassador-to-afp-general-headquarters","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/1a.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"506\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/1a.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>The Australian Ambassador to the Philippines, His Excellency Steven J Robinson AO and his delegation visited the General Headquarters, Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) in Camp Aguinaldo on Wednesday, June 8. His delegation was warmly welcomed by the AFP Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA.</p>\r\n<p>The Australian government continuous to be an active partner of the Philippines not only on defense and security but also in our effort in addressing the global pandemic.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/1a.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-09T16:58:44+08:00","hits":184},{"id":1161,"title":"PH-US conduct Marine Aviation Support Activity 2022 ","slug":"ph-us-conduct-marine-aviation-support-activity-2022","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/MASA_2022.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/MASA_2022.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Armed Forces of the Philippines through the Philippine Marine Corps and the United States Marine Corps Forces Pacific opened the Marine Aviation Support Activity 2022 (MASA 22) yesterday, June 6, at the PMC headquarters in Taguig City.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Activities commenced yesterday, June 6 in the province of Palawan and will end on June 17 that includes combined joint forward arming and refuelling demonstration, and a lecture on unmanned air systems operations.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/MASA_2022.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-08T17:03:01+08:00","hits":288},{"id":1162,"title":"AFP designates new Deputy Chief of Staff for CMO","slug":"afp-designates-new-deputy-chief-of-staff-for-cmo","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/285715932_375590847936665_4928248613826748105_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/285715932_375590847936665_4928248613826748105_n.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines installed Brigadier General Gabriel C Viray III PA as the new Deputy Chief of Staff for Civil Military Operations, J7 on Thursday, 02 June 2022. Brig. Gen. Viray III replaced Maj. Gen. Nolasco A Mempin who assumed as the Commander of the 10th Infantry Division in February.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\"Taking the helm of OJ7 is one of a lifetime experience. It provides me an opportunity to lead a highly motivated team, and an opportunity to serve our organization – the AFP, our stakeholders, the community that we engage in, and our country in general,\" Brig. Gen. Viray said.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/285715932_375590847936665_4928248613826748105_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-07T17:20:05+08:00","hits":1188},{"id":1163,"title":"AFP-PNP-PCG Little Olympics 2022 closes","slug":"afp-pnp-pcg-little-olympics-2022-closes","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/286396377_376825461146537_4520881915836462513_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/286396377_376825461146537_4520881915836462513_n.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - Athletes from the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), Philippine National Police (PNP) and Philippine Coast Guard (PCG) participated in the closing ceremony of this year’s Little Olympics on Friday, June 3 at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand in Camp Aguinaldo.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The first face-to-face AFP-PNP-PCG Little Olympics since the start of the COVID-19 pandemic was launched on May 24 to promote physical fitness and wellness among dependents of uniformed service members.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/286396377_376825461146537_4520881915836462513_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-07T17:14:00+08:00","hits":2169},{"id":1164,"title":"General Centino meets with India’s National Defense College chief, students","slug":"general-centino-meets-with-india-s-national-defense-college-chief-students","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/286532866_377553484407068_5431510396074846448_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/286532866_377553484407068_5431510396074846448_n.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP GENERAL EMILIO AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA met with Major General Manoj Kumar, other senior staff, and students of India’s National Defense College on Monday, 06 June 2022, at the General Headquarters here.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The meeting is part of a study tour aimed at providing the delegates, which included students from Sri Lanka, Uganda, Australia, Iran, and Uzbekistan; with an overview of the country’s socio-economic development, foreign policy, and security issues.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/286532866_377553484407068_5431510396074846448_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-07T17:06:43+08:00","hits":208},{"id":1165,"title":"General Centino lauds AFP’s judge advocates in 85th anniversary","slug":"general-centino-lauds-afp-s-judge-advocates-in-85th-anniversary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Office of the Judge Advocate General, Armed Forces of the Philippines celebrated its 85th Founding Anniversary with Supreme Court Associate Justice Japar B Dimaampao as Guest of Honor and Speaker.</p>\r\n<p><br />A ceremony was held today, 07 June 2022, at the Tejeros Hall here that highlighted the AFP’s lawyers’ contribution to the military since the establishment of the Judge Advocate General Service (JAGS) in 1935.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-07T17:04:50+08:00","hits":538},{"id":1166,"title":"The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP meets Nigerian Defense Attaché","slug":"the-deputy-chief-of-staff-afp-meets-nigerian-defense-attache","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/viber_image_2022-05-24_14-36-11-870.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/viber_image_2022-05-24_14-36-11-870.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Air Commodore Ehimen Ejodame paid a courtesy call to the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Deputy Chief of Staff on Tuesday, May 24.</p>\r\n<p>Vice Admiral Rommel Anthony SD Reyes received the Nigerian Defense Attaché to the Philippines at the AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/viber_image_2022-05-24_14-36-11-870.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-03T20:28:54+08:00","hits":191},{"id":1167,"title":"AFP receives care packages for troops, kids in West Philippine Sea","slug":"afp-receives-care-packages-for-troops-kids-in-west-philippine-sea","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/viber_image_2022-05-30_13-12-23-416.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/viber_image_2022-05-30_13-12-23-416.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) received 29 boxes of care packages from the University of the Philippines Cadet Alumni Organization (UPCAO) intended for soldiers and school children in the Kalayaan Island Group (KIG) fronting the West Philippine Sea in Palawan on Monday, May 30.</p>\r\n<p>Boxes of food supplies, drinking water, and toiletries will go to troops deployed in KIG detachments. Other goods such as milk, biscuits, school supplies and materials will be distributed to the children in the Islands that compose the Kalayaan Group.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/viber_image_2022-05-30_13-12-23-416.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-03T20:25:43+08:00","hits":210},{"id":1168,"title":"CA confirms promotion of 17 AFP Generals, Flag Officers","slug":"ca-confirms-promotion-of-17-afp-generals-flag-officers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/viber_image_2022-05-30_18-01-33-995.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/viber_image_2022-05-30_18-01-33-995.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Commission on Appointments (CA) on Monday approved the ad interim promotions of 17 Generals and Flag Officers of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP).</p>\r\n<p>The CA confirmed nine generals from the Philippine Army. They were Lieutenant General William N Gonzales, Major General Camilo Z Ligayo, Major General Wilbur C Mamawag, Major General Ignatius N Patrimonio, Major General Romulo A Manuel Jr, Brigadier General Adonis Ariel G Orio, Brigadier General Glenn Jun C Calambuhay, Brigadier General Consolito P Yecla, and Brigadier General Marvin L Licudine.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/viber_image_2022-05-30_18-01-33-995.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-03T17:29:45+08:00","hits":688},{"id":1169,"title":"AFP Chief lauds 'Tabak' warriors' victories against communist, local terrorists","slug":"afp-chief-lauds-tabak-warriors-victories-against-communist-local-terrorists","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/viber_image_2022-06-01_19-44-43-721.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/viber_image_2022-06-01_19-44-43-721.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) General Andres Centino commended the troops of the Army's 1st Infantry \"Tabak\" Division for carrying out successful operations against armed threats in South-Western Mindanao during the unit's 86th founding anniversary celebration in Labangan, Zamboanga del Sur on Wednesday, June 1.</p>\r\n<p>General Centino recognized 1ID's accomplishments which include the neutralization of 615 personalities from communist terrorists and local terrorist groups. Of the 615 neutralized personalities, 60 died in encounters, 358 were apprehended, and 197 surrendered. Moreover, 844 firearms were seized or surrendered, and four communist terrorist's guerrilla fronts were dismantled.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/viber_image_2022-06-01_19-44-43-721.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-03T17:28:03+08:00","hits":777},{"id":1170,"title":"AFP troops seize NPA Firearms in Quezon","slug":"afp-troops-seize-npa-firearms-in-quezon","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) seized high-powered firearms from the CPP-NPA Terrorist (CNT) in General Nakar, Quezon Province, on Wednesday, June 1.</p>\r\n<p>Members of the Philippine Army's 1st Infantry Battalion (1IB) seized an M16 rifle, hand grenade, anti-personnel mine, and subversive documents after an encounter with about 10 NPAs in Brgy. Magsikap.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-03T17:25:31+08:00","hits":277},{"id":1171,"title":"Soldiers seize terrorist's firearm, ammunition in Samar","slug":"soldiers-seize-terrorists-firearm-ammunition-in-samar","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--Troops of the Philippine Army's 78th Infantry Battalion under the 8th Infantry Division seized an M-16 rifle, three magazines, and 76 rounds of ammunition while conducting combat operations in Barangay Pinanag-an, Borongan City, Eastern Samar on Wednesday, 01 June 2022.</p>\r\n<p>The soldiers discovered the war materials while pursuing the communist terrorist group (CTG) operating in the area. The operating troops also seized one bandolier and one backpack believed to belong to fleeing CTG members.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-06-03T17:23:33+08:00","hits":168},{"id":1172,"title":"AFP hosts first face-to-face Little Olympics since pandemic","slug":"afp-hosts-first-face-to-face-little-olympics-since-pandemic","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June 2023/viber_image_2022-05-24_12-36-12-988.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/June 2023/viber_image_2022-05-24_12-36-12-988.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Dependents of uniformed service members and civilian employees join the Armed Forces of the Philippines-Philippine National Police-Philippine Coast Guard (AFP-PNP-PCG) Little Olympics on Tuesday, August 24.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The opening ceremony of the first face-to-face sporting event since the pandemic was held at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand in Camp Aguinaldo. It was joined by players aged 17 years old and below.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/June%202023/viber_image_2022-05-24_12-36-12-988.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-05-24T20:31:01+08:00","hits":156},{"id":1173,"title":"AFP Chief checks on troops in Balabac, Palawan","slug":"afp-chief-checks-on-troops-in-balabac-palawan","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May 2022/B.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/May 2022/B.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) visited one of the country's farthest detachments in Palawan and urged troops to further strengthen its security operations in the area.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">General Andres Centino flew to Bugsuk Island in Balabac, Palawan, on Thursday, May 19, as part of his regular troops' visitation, especially in far-flung military bases and detachments.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May%202022/B.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-05-20T20:34:54+08:00","hits":220},{"id":1174,"title":"AFP Chief meets PH Army Reservist Matteo Guidicelli","slug":"afp-chief-meets-ph-army-reservist-matteo-guidicelli-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"a54g7\" data-offset-key=\"41pkj-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"41pkj-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"41pkj-0-0\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May 2022/viber_image_2022-05-19_08-43-03-080.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/May 2022/viber_image_2022-05-19_08-43-03-080.jpg\" /></span></div>\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"41pkj-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"41pkj-0-0\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Actor-singer Matteo Guidicelli paid a courtesy call to Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Chief of Staff Andres Centino at the General Headquarters Building in Camp Aguinaldo on Wednesday, May 18.</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"a54g7\" data-offset-key=\"cru2-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"cru2-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"cru2-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"cru2-0-0\"> </span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May%202022/viber_image_2022-05-19_08-43-03-080.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-05-19T20:43:26+08:00","hits":1097},{"id":1175,"title":"AFP Chief meets PH Army Reservist Matteo Guidicelli","slug":"afp-chief-meets-ph-army-reservist-matteo-guidicelli","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"a54g7\" data-offset-key=\"41pkj-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"41pkj-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"41pkj-0-0\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May 2022/viber_image_2022-05-19_08-43-03-080.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/May 2022/viber_image_2022-05-19_08-43-03-080.jpg\" /></span></div>\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"41pkj-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"41pkj-0-0\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Actor-singer Matteo Guidicelli paid a courtesy call to Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Chief of Staff Andres Centino at the General Headquarters Building in Camp Aguinaldo on Wednesday, May 18.</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"a54g7\" data-offset-key=\"cru2-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"cru2-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"cru2-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"cru2-0-0\"> </span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May%202022/viber_image_2022-05-19_08-43-03-080.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-05-19T20:40:05+08:00","hits":217},{"id":1176,"title":"AFP Chief lauds 5ID’s gains against Communist Terrorists in Northern Luzon","slug":"afp-chief-lauds-5id-s-gains-against-communist-terrorists-in-northern-luzon","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May 2022/viber_image_2022-05-18_10-50-15-960.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/May 2022/viber_image_2022-05-18_10-50-15-960.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) lauded the members of the Philippine Army's 5th Infantry \"Star\" Division for its successful campaign against the Communist Terrorist Group (CTG) in Northern Luzon.</p>\r\n<p>\"With the active participation of the Star Division in our whole of nation approach, the people of Ilocos, Cagayan Valley, and Cordillera Administrative Region felt significant economic progress, as well as peace and security in their communities,\" said General Andres Centino.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May%202022/viber_image_2022-05-18_10-50-15-960.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-05-18T20:45:06+08:00","hits":162},{"id":1177,"title":"AFP Statement on Republic Act 11709 prescribing three-year fixed terms for AFP Officials","slug":"afp-statement-on-republic-act-11709-prescribing-three-year-fixed-terms-for-afp-officials","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May 2022/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/May 2022/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>The leadership of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) welcomes President Rodrigo Duterte’s approval of the prescribed three-year fixed terms for military officials holding key positions.</p>\r\n<p>The AFP is confident that the newly-signed law will bring stability in the military organization as we continue to fulfil our mandate as protectors of the people and the state.</p>\r\n<p>We are grateful for the support of the administration as well as the Senate and the House of Representatives in ensuring the continuity of our programs and operations.</p>\r\n<p>This shall make the AFP a more efficient and effective organization and will contribute to the realization of our vision of a more credible Armed Forces which is a source of national pride. ///</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May%202022/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-05-17T20:48:06+08:00","hits":182},{"id":1178,"title":"AFP holds First Football Festival since the pandemic","slug":"afp-holds-first-football-festival-since-the-pandemic","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May 2022/9EAD91D8-282A-4682-BA4B-A7B37E9EB51F.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/May 2022/9EAD91D8-282A-4682-BA4B-A7B37E9EB51F.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) held its first face-to-face Football Festival since the start of the pandemic on Saturday, May 14.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP Office of the Deputy Chief of Staff for Reservist and Retiree Affairs (OJ9) headed by Major General Camilo Ligayo, spearheaded the sporting event conducted at Fort Bonifacio Naval Station Parade Ground in Taguig City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May%202022/9EAD91D8-282A-4682-BA4B-A7B37E9EB51F.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-05-14T20:50:56+08:00","hits":202},{"id":1179,"title":"5 NPAs surrender to AFP in Agusan del Sur","slug":"5-npas-surrender-to-afp-in-agusan-del-sur","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May 2022/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/May 2022/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – After experiencing hardship with the Communist Terrorist New People’s Army (NPA), five members voluntarily surrendered to the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) in Agusan del Sur on Monday, May 9.</p>\r\n<p>Members of the Army’s 3rd Special Forces Battalion facilitated the surrender of Alias Bebe, Alias Rowel, Alias Jenny, Alias Rey, and Alias Joy (true name withheld for their protection)</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May%202022/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-05-11T20:53:28+08:00","hits":168},{"id":1180,"title":"AFP receives Php6 Million scholarship grant from PVAO","slug":"afp-receives-php6-million-scholarship-grant-from-pvao","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May 2022/1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"723\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/May 2022/1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) received P6,000,000.00 in monetary donations from the Philippine Veterans Affairs Office (PVAO) for the educational benefits of military personnel and their dependents.</p>\r\n<p>A ceremonial signing of the memorandum of agreement and turnover of check donation was held at PVAO in Camp Aguinaldo on Wednesday, May 4.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May%202022/1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-05-06T21:00:30+08:00","hits":290},{"id":1181,"title":"AFP receives Hawker Aircraft from San Miguel Corporation","slug":"afp-receives-hawker-aircraft-from-san-miguel-corporation","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May 2022/viber_image_2022-05-06_10-43-24-365.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"517\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/May 2022/viber_image_2022-05-06_10-43-24-365.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) received a Beechcraft Hawker Aircraft donated by the San Miguel Corporation (SMC) on Thursday, May 5.</p>\r\n<p>A formal acceptance, turnover, and blessing ceremony was presided over by Defense Secretary Delfin Lorenzana at the Villamor Air Base in Pasay City. He was joined by SMC Chief Executive Officer, Ramon Ang.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May%202022/viber_image_2022-05-06_10-43-24-365.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-05-06T20:58:08+08:00","hits":259},{"id":1182,"title":"NPA surrender in Bukidnon, firearms seized in Davao de Oro","slug":"npa-surrender-in-bukidnon-firearms-seized-in-davao-de-oro","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May 2022/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/May 2022/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – A member of a dismantled guerrilla unit of the communist terrorist New People’s Army (NPA) surrendered to the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) in Bukidnon.</p>\r\n<p>A certain Sander Langayed using the alias ‘Anggot’ yielded to the 89th Infantry Battalion at Sitio Inayaman, Brgy San Jose, San Fernando, Bukidnon. He also turned in an M1 Garand rifle, M203 grenade launcher and anti-personnel mine.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May%202022/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-05-06T20:55:57+08:00","hits":221},{"id":1183,"title":"Premier Army Engineer helps repair historic Veterans Center","slug":"premier-army-engineer-helps-repair-historic-veterans-center","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May 2022/viber_image_2022-05-05_14-41-51-585.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/May 2022/viber_image_2022-05-05_14-41-51-585.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>The 51st Engineer Brigade, one of the Philippine Army’s premier engineering arms, successfully renovated and repaired the old Filipino Veterans Center inside the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.</p>\r\n<p>Led by Brigadier General JT Bajet, the men and women of the 51EBde labored to make the old structure a towering reminder of Filipino nationalism and patriotism in time for its inauguration on April 13, 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May%202022/viber_image_2022-05-05_14-41-51-585.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-05-06T08:02:26+08:00","hits":188},{"id":1184,"title":"AFP Chief boards Navy ship boosts personnel morale","slug":"afp-chief-boards-navy-ship-boosts-personnel-morale","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May 2022/E5E2D982-BDAF-4813-951F-8037DF037E06.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/May 2022/E5E2D982-BDAF-4813-951F-8037DF037E06.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA uplifted the morale of BRP Tausug (LC-295) personnel as he boarded the naval ship on Saturday, April 30, 2022.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP Chief of Staff was received aboard by CDR ALLAN ROY D CANILANG PN, Commanding Officer, BRP Tausug (LC-295) in Magallanes Port, Limasawa, Southern Leyte.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May%202022/E5E2D982-BDAF-4813-951F-8037DF037E06.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-05-05T08:21:29+08:00","hits":218},{"id":1185,"title":"AFP joins Multi-Agency Send-Off Ceremony of Security Forces","slug":"afp-joins-multi-agency-send-off-ceremony-of-security-forces","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May 2022/viber_image_2022-05-04_11-32-42-752.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/May 2022/viber_image_2022-05-04_11-32-42-752.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Less than a week before the National and Local Elections, the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) joined government agencies in sending off forces to be deployed for election duties on Wednesday, May 4.</p>\r\n<p>The multi-agency send-off and turnover ceremony was held at the Philippine National Police (PNP) Grandstand in Camp Crame, Quezon City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May%202022/viber_image_2022-05-04_11-32-42-752.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-05-04T08:12:28+08:00","hits":299},{"id":1186,"title":"NPA fighter killed in Masbate Encounter, Firearm Captured","slug":"npa-fighter-killed-in-masbate-encounter-firearm-captured","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May 2022/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/May 2022/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – A member of the communist terrorist New People’s Army (NPA) was killed in an encounter with Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) troops in Palanas, Masbate on Monday, May 2.</p>\r\n<p>Operating troops from the Philippine Army’s 2nd Infantry Battalion encountered the NPA member along with four others at Brgy. San Isidro in Palanas.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May%202022/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-05-04T08:10:01+08:00","hits":266},{"id":1187,"title":"Terrorist NPA killed in Negros Occidental Firefight","slug":"terrorist-npa-killed-in-negros-occidental-firefight","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May 2022/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/May 2022/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – A communist terrorist New People's Army (NPA) was killed in a firefight with AFP troops in Negros Occidental on Tuesday, May 3.</p>\r\n<p>Responding to the report of concerned citizens on the presence of the armed group in their barangays, operating troops of the Philippine Army's 15th Infantry Battalion under the 3rd Infantry Division encountered about five NPAs in Barangay Gatuslao, Candoni, Negros Occidental.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May%202022/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-05-04T08:05:41+08:00","hits":205},{"id":1188,"title":"AFP receives over $2.3 Million in equipment grants from U.S. Gov’t","slug":"afp-receives-over-2-3-million-in-equipment-grants-from-u-s-gov-t","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May 2022/58E181D1-B9F0-4EAB-BFB3-655CC0596D47.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/May 2022/58E181D1-B9F0-4EAB-BFB3-655CC0596D47.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) received $2,304,728.39 worth of equipment grant from the United States government on Monday, May 2.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The various defense equipment arrived at the Haribon Terminal, Clark Air Base in Pampanga via a U.S. KC-10A aircraft. Upon its unloading, Supply Officers from the AFP Major Services inspected the hardware.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May%202022/58E181D1-B9F0-4EAB-BFB3-655CC0596D47.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-05-03T08:18:50+08:00","hits":233},{"id":1189,"title":"AFP seizes NPA firearms in Samar encounter","slug":"afp-seizes-npa-firearms-in-samar-encounter","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May 2022/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/May 2022/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The 63rd Infantry Battalion under the 8th Infantry Division of the Philippine Army figured in an encounter with suspected members of the Communist Terrorist Group NPA on Monday, May 2.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Troops conducting Focused Military Operations clashed against nine (9) personalities believed to be members of BUGSOK Pltn, SRC, SESAME at Sitio Lanaga, Barangay Cancaiyas, Basey, Samar.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/May%202022/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-05-03T08:15:03+08:00","hits":209},{"id":1190,"title":"AFP, Stakeholders donate almost P1 Million to rebuild Limasawa Island","slug":"afp-stakeholders-donate-almost-p1-million-to-rebuild-limasawa-island","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/0430 AFP Stakeholders donate almost P1 Million to rebuild Limasawa Island.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/0430 AFP Stakeholders donate almost P1 Million to rebuild Limasawa Island.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and its partner stakeholders turned over construction materials worth P950,000.00 to the people of Limasawa Island, Southern Leyte on Saturday, April 30.<br /><br />The donated items came from the proceeds of the recently concluded ‘Heroes Adventure Challenge: Race to Rebuild Limasawa’ organized by Ms. Theresa Mae Conson of Smarties Apparel and Active Hub Events and Wellness. It sought to help the victims of Typhoon Odette through the reconstruction of their homes.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/0430%20AFP%20Stakeholders%20donate%20almost%20P1%20Million%20to%20rebuild%20Limasawa%20Island.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-30T09:32:26+08:00","hits":200},{"id":1191,"title":"2 NPAs killed in Surigao Sur encounter","slug":"2-npas-killed-in-surigao-sur-encounter","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/0429 2 NPAs killed in Surigao Sur encounter.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/0429 2 NPAs killed in Surigao Sur encounter.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">City - Two members of the communist terrorist New People's Army (CNTs) were killed in an encounter with soldiers of the 36th Infantry battalion on Friday, April 29 in Lanuza, Surigao del Sur.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Army's 4th Infantry Division said troops belonging to 36th IB under the 901st Infantry Brigade<br />while conducting security operations figured in a five minutes encounter with more or less 10 communist rebels believed to be members of Guerilla Front 30 of the North Eastern Mindanao Regional Committee (NEMRC) at Sitio Catupgas Brgy Nurcia, Lanuza.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/0429%202%20NPAs%20killed%20in%20Surigao%20Sur%20encounter.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-29T09:29:28+08:00","hits":238},{"id":1192,"title":"2 NPAs yield, surrender firearms to AFP","slug":"2-npas-yield-surrender-firearms-to-afp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04292022 2 NPAs yield surrender firearms to AFP.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04292022 2 NPAs yield surrender firearms to AFP.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Two NPA rebels in Quezon surrendered on April 27, 2022, as a result of joint military operations and successful delivery of government services.</p>\r\n<p>Joint elements of the 85th Infantry Battalion, 59th Infantry Battalion, and 83rd Infantry Battalion facilitated the surrender in Sitio Buli, Brgr. Castañas, Sariaya, Quezon.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04292022%202%20NPAs%20yield%20surrender%20firearms%20to%20AFP.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-29T09:24:03+08:00","hits":222},{"id":1193,"title":"AFP Chief lauds Engineer Brigade in Cebu","slug":"afp-chief-lauds-engineer-brigade-in-cebu","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04292022 AFP Chief lauds Engineer Brigade in Cebu.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04292022 AFP Chief lauds Engineer Brigade in Cebu.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) lauded the men and women of the Engineer Brigade based in Cebu City for their disaster response efforts after the recent typhoons.</p>\r\n<p>General Centino was in Camp Lapulapu to check on the state of morale of troops assigned at the 53rd Engineer Brigade. He was received by its Commander, Colonel Proceso Rebancos.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04292022%20AFP%20Chief%20lauds%20Engineer%20Brigade%20in%20Cebu.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-29T09:22:11+08:00","hits":226},{"id":1194,"title":"AFP Chief visits Naval Forces Central, commends troops","slug":"afp-chief-visits-naval-forces-central-commends-troops","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p> </p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUIN<img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04292022 AFP Chief visits Naval Forces Central commends troops.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04292022 AFP Chief visits Naval Forces Central commends troops.jpg\" />ALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) visited the Naval Forces Central (NAVFORCEN) in the Visayas to commend troops for their disaster response efforts during typhoons.</p>\r\n<p>General Andres Centino was at the Naval Base Rafael Ramos in Brgy. Looc, Lapu-Lapu City on Thursday, April 28, for a traditional command visit and talk to troops. He was received by its Commander, Commodore Florante Gagua.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04292022%20AFP%20Chief%20visits%20Naval%20Forces%20Central%20commends%20troops.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-29T09:12:10+08:00","hits":196},{"id":1195,"title":"AFP joins 501st anniversary of the Victory of Mactan","slug":"afp-joins-501st-anniversary-of-the-victory-of-mactan","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04292022 AFP joins 501st anniversary of the Victory of Mactan.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04292022 AFP joins 501st anniversary of the Victory of Mactan.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) joined the 501st anniversary celebration of the Victory of Mactan at the Liberty Shrine in Lapu-Lapu City on April 27, 2021.</p>\r\n<p>The event sought to commemorate the victory of Lapulapu and his men over the Spaniards in the historic Battle of Mactan on April 27, 1521.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04292022%20AFP%20joins%20501st%20anniversary%20of%20the%20Victory%20of%20Mactan.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-29T09:09:39+08:00","hits":169},{"id":1196,"title":"AFP joins 2022 Asian Defense & Security Exhibition","slug":"afp-joins-2022-asian-defense-security-exhibition","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04272022 AFP joins 2022 Asian Defense  Security Exhibition.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04272022 AFP joins 2022 Asian Defense  Security Exhibition.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City</strong> – To update and evaluate its modernization program requirements, the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) joined this year’s Asian Defense &amp; Security (ADAS) exhibition happening in Pasay City from 27 to 29 April 2022.</p>\r\n<p>The AFP Chief of Staff, General Andres Centino attended the ADAS 2022 opening ceremony at the World Trade Center Metro Manila on Wednesday. In a message, he cited the event as an opportunity for the AFP’s project evaluation teams to assess and evaluate suitable requirements for the military’s defense and security platforms, systems, and equipment.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04272022%20AFP%20joins%202022%20Asian%20Defense%20%20Security%20Exhibition.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-27T09:05:10+08:00","hits":254},{"id":1197,"title":"2 NPAs killed, firearms seized in Occidental Mindoro","slug":"2-npas-killed-firearms-seized-in-occidental-mindoro","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Two members of the communist terrorist New People’s Army (NPA) were killed while four high-powered firearms were seized in a series of military operations in Occidental Mindoro on Monday, April 25.</p>\r\n<p>The first encounter occurred in the morning as combined elements of the Army’s 68th Infantry Battalion, and Philippine National Police Special Action Force clashed with about 10 NPAs in Brgy. Malpalon, Calintaan, Occidental Mindoro.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-26T08:59:45+08:00","hits":192},{"id":1198,"title":"2 Communist Terrorists fall, firearms captured in Masbate encounter","slug":"2-communist-terrorists-fall-firearms-captured-in-masbate-encounter","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) troops neutralized two members of the communist terrorist New People’s Army in a fierce firefight on Monday, April 25.</p>\r\n<p>Combined forces led by the Army’s 2nd Infantry Battalion, while on security operations encountered more or less 20 NPA fighters at the vicinity of Brgy. Miabas, Palanas, Masbate.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-26T08:57:26+08:00","hits":193},{"id":1199,"title":"AFP gets construction equipment from GMA Kapuso Foundation","slug":"afp-gets-construction-equipment-from-gma-kapuso-foundation","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04252022 AFP gets construction equipment from GMA Kapuso Foundation.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04252022 AFP gets construction equipment from GMA Kapuso Foundation.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) received new construction equipment for restoring damaged military camps and patrol bases on Monday, April 25.</p>\r\n<p>The GMA Kapuso Foundation (GMAKF) donation will benefit the units severely affected by Typhoon Odette in December 2021.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04252022%20AFP%20gets%20construction%20equipment%20from%20GMA%20Kapuso%20Foundation.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-25T08:54:51+08:00","hits":310},{"id":1200,"title":"AFP Chief meets long-time foe after 14 years","slug":"afp-chief-meets-long-time-foe-after-14-years","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04252022 AFP Chief meets long-time foe after 14 years.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04252022 AFP Chief meets long-time foe after 14 years.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Fourteen years since he vowed to hunt down a notorious communist terrorist leader, former Battalion Commander and now the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) met his long-time foe in Davao de Oro on Saturday, April 23.</p>\r\n<p>General Andres Centino met Maximo Catarata Alias Datu Makatindog, the former highest ranking leader of the weakened Guerilla Front 3 of the New People’s Army (NPA) during his visit at the 10th Infantry Division headquarters in Camp General Manuel T Yan Sr., Tuboran, Mawab, Davao de Oro.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04252022%20AFP%20Chief%20meets%20long-time%20foe%20after%2014%20years.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-25T08:48:27+08:00","hits":246},{"id":1201,"title":"AFP Chief inspects military facilities in Philippines' southernmost island municipality","slug":"afp-chief-inspects-military-facilities-in-philippines-southernmost-island-municipality","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04252022 AFP Chief inspects military facilities in Philippines southernmost island municipality.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04252022 AFP Chief inspects military facilities in Philippines southernmost island municipality.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino inspected the military’s Mabila Detachment and Littoral Monitoring Station in Balut Island, Saranggani on April 23, 2022.</p>\r\n<p>These facilities are situated in one of the most remote and southernmost municipalities in the Philippines that serve as early warning and detection for incoming vessels in the country's domain.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04252022%20AFP%20Chief%20inspects%20military%20facilities%20in%20Philippines%20southernmost%20island%20municipality.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-25T08:42:27+08:00","hits":200},{"id":1202,"title":"AFP Chief commends troops in Davao de Oro for the steady decline of Insurgents","slug":"afp-chief-commends-troops-in-davao-de-oro-for-the-steady-decline-of-insurgents","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04252022 AFP Chief commends troops in Davao de Oro for the steady decline of Insurgents.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"559\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04252022 AFP Chief commends troops in Davao de Oro for the steady decline of Insurgents.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Chief of Staff Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) General Andres C Centino commended the troops of the 48th Infantry ‘Guardians’ Battalion for its significant strides against the Communist Terrorist Groups (CTGs).</p>\r\n<p>“I am pleased to note that we are successfully clearing your area from the insurgents. I express my commendation to you for being able to contribute to the mission of the AFP to ensure that we have secured communities all over the country,” he said.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04252022%20AFP%20Chief%20commends%20troops%20in%20Davao%20de%20Oro%20for%20the%20steady%20decline%20of%20Insurgents.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-25T08:28:00+08:00","hits":299},{"id":1203,"title":"AFP seizes thousands of NPA ammunition, firearms in Sorsogon","slug":"afp-seizes-thousands-of-npa-ammunition-firearms-in-sorsogon","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04222022 AFP seizes thousands of NPA ammunition firearms in Sorsogon.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04222022 AFP seizes thousands of NPA ammunition firearms in Sorsogon.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) seized thousands of ammunition and firearms owned by the communist terrorist group (CTG) in Sorsogon on April 21.</p>\r\n<p>Lt. Col. Nelson Mico, Commanding Officer of 22nd Infantry Battalion (22IB) under the 903rd Brigade of the 9th Infantry Division, Philippine Army, reported that his troops discovered the CTG’s armed cache at the hinterland areas of Barangay Capi, Bulan through the report of concerned civilians.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04222022%20AFP%20seizes%20thousands%20of%20NPA%20ammunition%20firearms%20in%20Sorsogon.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-22T08:20:55+08:00","hits":385},{"id":1204,"title":"3 terrorist NPAs yield in Masbate","slug":"3-terrorist-npas-yield-in-masbate-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr 2022/04222022 3 terrorist NPAs yield in Masbate.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Apr 2022/04222022 3 terrorist NPAs yield in Masbate.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Three communist terrorist NPAs (CNTs) yielded to the Philippine Army’s 2nd Infantry Battalion (2IB) of the 9th Infantry Division in Masbate on April 21, 2022.</p>\r\n<p>According to Lt. Col. Siegfried Felipe F Awichen, Commanding Officer of 2IB, after a series of negotiation, his troops was able to convince Alias Pinoy, Alias Darwin, and Alias Nikoy to lay down their arms and heed the government’s call for peace by availing the Enhanced Comprehensive Local Integration Program (E-CLIP) of the government.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Apr%202022/04222022%203%20terrorist%20NPAs%20yield%20in%20Masbate.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-22T08:17:18+08:00","hits":176},{"id":1205,"title":"2 terrorist NPAs killed in Quezon encounter","slug":"2-terrorist-npas-killed-in-quezon-encounter-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - Two communist terrorist NPAs (CNTs) were killed in an encounter with government troops in Quezon province on April 18.</p>\r\n<p>While conducting security operations at Sito Angelo, Barangay Umiray, General Nakar on Monday afternoon, troops from the Philippine Army's 24th Division Reconnaissance Company under the 2nd Infantry Division chanced upon the more or less seven CNTs, resulting in a firefight.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-04-20T08:13:08+08:00","hits":166}]}